PRETABLE -- #529 kill table 10 (TARGETED, repair 12), written BEFORE the table (mtime is the order proof)
Instrument: regress/crime_width_probe.py after REPAIR 12, frozen by the driver as crime_width_probe.table10.py -- 157 rows
(141 + 16).  Fixed build: 157/157, CRIMEP_CONTROL=OK (../probe_first13_fix.out, build/gxemul, dev_sgi_ip32.c CMP_CLEAN).

WHAT CHANGED SINCE TABLE 9 (the flagship ruling on closing pass 6, regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/FABLE_C4_RULING_20260915.md,
part A): NO existing session's command list changed.  Added: `latch said' (a new ROW reading latch x5's existing
transcript -- codex's repair, the FLOOR row for the announced accept-guard-growth class); `free revP said' (one new
free-running session, a licensed strengthening); four new sessions of VALUE rows at the twelve cells the silent form is
guest-visible at (revP sw/sd/ld pc; acc ctl ld, acc istat ld, acc imask sw, acc time sd, acc 40 lw, acc 40 sw, acc ctl sd;
istw pre/sd/mid/sw); free_one() honours `clean'; header items 3/5/6/9 and five DISCLOSED bullets rewritten.

TARGETING.  The rule (re-run an earlier kill iff every row it last reddened sits in a session whose command list changed)
selects NOTHING: no command list changed.  But `latch said' is a new row in latch x5, and the flagship ruling (RA2) owes the
table the pre-set kills IF their scores are to be recorded -- they are, because the Opus seat's "they also red latch said"
is REASONED, not measured.  So: the 17 table-9 kills whose red set is {latch x5}; the Opus sixth-closing seat's C1, C2 and
G1-G6 from its mutator copied as run (mutants_c6_opus.py); a SILENT BYPASS at each of the twelve value-row cells (each
value row owes a MEASURED kill); and the d->warned-keyed accept shrink in both forms (RA3).  40 legs, FOUR probe lanes.

